    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_606d9394",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: stop_using_others_cultures_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman holding a drum in a grassy outdoor setting, with overlaid text that reads 'stop using other's cultures to fill up your empty white settler soul.' The overall intent is to deliver a hateful message targeting white settlers, implying that their cultural appropriation is a sign of emptiness or moral deficiency. This is a racially charged and culturally insensitive statement that attacks a specific racial group (white settlers) by suggesting their cultural engagement is inherently flawed and morally bankrupt. The meme uses the visual of a woman (who may be perceived as representing a 'white settler' or 'white culture') juxtaposed with the text to reinforce a message of racial superiority and cultural ownership, which is a form of hate speech directed at a specific racial group. The meme is designed to provoke anger or shame in its target audience and to reinforce a narrative of racial hierarchy and cultural appropriation as a moral failing.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_02ec73a3"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
